  "numbers": "Limits, defaults, ranges, times and ratios. Use 'tables' on DNSLimitations and adopt each needed row with its header '| Entity | Quota |' (hosted zones per account, records per zone, VPCs per private hosted zone, health checks per account, Resolver endpoint and rule quotas, Profiles). Quote whole sentences for the rest: number of name servers in a delegation set, weight range and weight 0, geoproximity bias range, multivalue maximum of healthy records, health check interval values, failure threshold default and range, the 18% rule, the TCP connect and response time limits, string-matching byte count, child health checks per calculated check, Resolver endpoint IP addresses and queries per second, Amazon-provided DNS addresses, recommended TTL values. One value per fact.",
  "behavior": "Can, cannot, only, always, by default, what happens when. Alias versus CNAME rules, zone apex, alias targets and TTL, each routing policy and its behavior with health checks, private hosted zone rules (VPC DNS settings, cross-account association, overlapping namespaces), health check types and evaluate target health, active-active versus active-passive, all-unhealthy behavior, VPC Resolver endpoints and forwarding rules, DNS Firewall actions, query logging destinations, domain registration and DNS migration, DNSSEC key requirements. One quoted sentence per claim. Work in the two batches given; write behavior-a facts first.",
